# Registry of paid benefits the paywall is allowed to advertise.
#
# Every bullet in `SubscriptionView.planCard(features:)` must appear here, and
# every entry here must still point at code that withholds the benefit from the
# free tier. `scripts/check_paywall_claims.sh` enforces both directions.
#
# Format — four pipe-separated fields:
#   <L10n symbol> | <file that enforces it> | <pattern that must still be there> | <what a free user loses>
#
# TWO tests, not one. A bullet earns its place only if BOTH hold:
#   (1) WITHHELD — some code refuses the benefit to a free user. That is what
#       the pattern field pins, and what this script can check mechanically.
#   (2) DELIVERED — a paying user actually receives it. This script CANNOT
#       check that, so it is on you, and it is the one that has already caught
#       something: `teamWorkspaces` passed test (1) — `TeamView` genuinely gates
#       on `isProOrAbove` — and failed test (2), because a production check
#       found that only `my_teams` of the eight team RPCs the client calls is
#       deployed. A Pro subscriber tapping "Create Team" hits a function that
#       does not exist. It was drafted into this file and pulled before merge.
#
# So: before adding a line, go look at the thing working for a paid account.
# "I found the gate" is half an answer.
#
# `everythingInPro` is deliberately absent: it is a pointer to the Pro card, not
# a benefit of its own. It is exempted by name in the checker.

unlimitedProviders | CLI Pulse Bar/CLIPulseCore/Sources/CLIPulseCore/AppState.swift | if currentEnabled >= maxProviders { | free tier cannot enable a 4th distinct provider kind; over-limit accounts are pruned to 3 on sign-in
homeScreenWidgets  | CLI Pulse Bar/CLI Pulse Widgets/UsageOverviewWidget.swift      | entry.data.isPro == false            | free tier gets WidgetProLockedView instead of the home-screen widget
homeScreenWidgets  | CLI Pulse Bar/CLI Pulse Widgets/LockScreenWidget.swift         | entry.data.isPro == false            | free tier gets the locked lock-screen widget
